# Tic-Tac-Toe
Two players take turns, X then O, putting their mark in an empty square.
Three in a row, across, down or corner to corner, wins;  nine marks and no row is a draw.
A square is this project's own, in `Square.spellml`;
this file holds the game, its board, and what a click on a square does.

<spell-app "tic tac toe">
	<property "board">a new board</>
	<property "turn" description="Whose turn it is:  X or O">text</>
	<property "winner" description="Who won:  X, O, nobody for a draw, or empty while the game goes on">text</>
	<alias "is over">if its winner is not ""</>
	<property "message" description="What the line above the board says">
		its turn + " to play" if its winner is ""
		"A draw" if its winner is "nobody"
		its winner + " wins!" otherwise
	</property>

	<action "create it" description="Nine squares, made with the game">
		// inside the loop `it` is the count:  so the board is the game's, by name
		repeat 9 times
			add a new square to tic tac toe's board
	</action>

	<group "playing"/>
	<action "start a new game" shortcut="N" description="An empty board, X to play">
		for square in its board
			set the square's mark to ""
		set its turn to "X"
		clear its winner
	</action>
	<spell>
		// the same mark in all three squares wins
		- to check the line from square (a as a number) through (b as a number) to (c as a number):
			set mark to the mark of square a of its board
			if mark is "" return
			if the mark of square b of its board is mark and the mark of square c of its board is mark
				set its winner to mark
	</spell>
	<action "check for a winner" description="Three in a row:  each row, each column, and the two diagonals;  a full board with none is a draw">
		check the line from square 1 through 2 to 3
		check the line from square 4 through 5 to 6
		check the line from square 7 through 8 to 9
		check the line from square 1 through 4 to 7
		check the line from square 2 through 5 to 8
		check the line from square 3 through 6 to 9
		check the line from square 1 through 5 to 9
		check the line from square 3 through 5 to 7
		if its winner is "" and its board has no squares where it is empty
			set its winner to "nobody"
	</action>

	<draw description="The message, the board three squares a row, then a button for a new game">
		<stack align="center">
			<card>
				<content>
					<header level="2" align="center">{its message}</header>
					{draw its board}
				</content>
				<content>
					<button fluid color="primary" onClick={start a new game}>New game</button>
				</content>
			</card>
		</stack>
	</draw>
</spell-app>

## Playing a square
What a click on a square does, added to this project's square:  `<spell-more-of>` adds to a type another file declares.

<spell-more-of "square">
	<action "play it" description="The turn's mark goes in the square, if it's empty and nobody has won;  then it's the other player's turn">
		if tic tac toe is over or it is not empty return
		set its mark to tic tac toe's turn
		check for a winner
		set tic tac toe's turn to "O" if tic tac toe's turn is "X" otherwise "X"
	</action>
</spell-more-of>

## The board
Nine squares, three a row:  square 1 top left, square 9 bottom right.
It draws each square as a big button, its mark in the mark's color;  a click plays it.

<spell-thing "board" template="list of squares">
	<draw>
		<for square in it as="grid" columns="3" spacing="compact">
			<column>
				<button fluid size="massive" appearance="basic" color={the color of the square} onClick={play the square}>
					{the label of the square}
				</button>
			</column>
		</for>
	</draw>
</spell-thing>

<spell>
	// a square is on one board
	a square belongs to one board
</spell>

## Start, and a test

<spell>
	start a new game

	to test three in a row
		start a new game
		play square 1 of tic tac toe's board
		play square 4 of tic tac toe's board
		play square 2 of tic tac toe's board
		play square 5 of tic tac toe's board
		play square 3 of tic tac toe's board
		tic tac toe's winner should be "X"
		tic tac toe's message should be "X wins!"
		the color of square 1 of tic tac toe's board should be "blue"
		start a new game
</spell>
